course: dictionary
lesson: 8309
title: Roam: moving around freely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Roam means to walk or travel around with no fixed plan, often over a wide area. «Wild lions have lost most of the land they once roamed across Africa.» The lions did not walk along one set path. They went wherever they liked over a big area, so roamed means moved around freely.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Polar bears roam huge distances, so they need deep, cool water and lots of space.» Huge distances and lots of space tell you that roam is about moving over a large area, not staying in one place.
explain: Roam also has other meanings. On a phone, «roaming charges» are the costs of using your phone abroad through another network. Eyes and thoughts can roam too, moving from place to place. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, check which one fits the sentence.
fact: Roam means to walk or travel around with no fixed plan, often over a wide area.
fact: Roams is used with he, she or it, and roamed is the past tense: «Mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world.»
fact: On a phone, roaming means using it abroad through another network, and it can cost a lot.
fact: Eyes or thoughts can roam too, moving from place to place.
fact: «Free to roam» and «roam the streets» are common phrases that show moving about without a fixed plan.
exercise: «Wild horses roam in Australia.» What does roam mean here? | *Walk or travel around with no fixed plan | Run in a race only once | Stay still in one small pen | Sleep under a roof
exercise: Mum says, «Check the roaming charges before you use your phone abroad.» What does roaming mean? | *Using a phone abroad through another network | Being lost inside the house | Playing games on a phone | Sending a text to a friend
exercise: Find the past tense of roam. | roam | roams | roaming | *roamed
test: «Werribee is a huge open-range zoo where giraffes and zebras roam large areas.» What does roam suggest about the animals? | They are painted in stripes | They are stuck in small pens | *They move freely over a big space | They sleep all day
test: Which sentence uses roam for thoughts? | Her thoughts were locked in a box | *Her thoughts roamed back to her summer holiday | Her thoughts stopped at the bus stop | Her thoughts were hungry and cold
exam: «Mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world.» What does widely tell you about roamed? | They were kept safe in zoos | *They moved over a large area | They stayed in one cave all their lives | They were very small animals
